<item><title>Swakopmund overtakes Windhoek in October building approvals as commercial projects slump</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/swakopmund-overtakes-windhoek-in-october-building-approvals-405dc3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/swakopmund-overtakes-windhoek-in-october-building-approvals-405dc3/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>Simonis Storm Research says Swakopmund approved N$209.8 million in plans in October, against N$187.4 million in Windhoek, as combined values fell 29.4%.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:47:14 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia needs 3,600 dairy cows to close 13.3 million-litre milk gap</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-needs-3-600-dairy-cows-to-close-13-3-million-litre-30b1a4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-needs-3-600-dairy-cows-to-close-13-3-million-litre-30b1a4/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>Agriculture Minister Inge Zaamwani told Parliament that 2025 production met 56% of demand, with imports from South Africa covering much of the shortfall.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:50:31 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
